# Walkthrough against the demo data in data.sql (fresh start).

### 4. Portfolio of seeded trader T001 -> AAPL 150, NVDA 100, TSLA 80; TECH 330
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/traders/T001/portfolio

### 5. Overlap -> TECH_HEAVY 75.00%, FINANCE_HEAVY 0.00%, BALANCED 50.00%, HIGH
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/traders/T001/portfolio/overlap

### 2. Fill seeded PENDING order #2 (BUY MSFT 20) -> MSFT appears in T001's portfolio
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders/2/fill

### 3. Cancel seeded PENDING order #3 (SELL AAPL 50)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders/3/cancel

### 3. Cancelling FILLED order #1 -> 409 INVALID_ORDER_STATE
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders/1/cancel

### 1. Place a BUY order for a brand-new trader (created automatically)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "traderId": "T004", "stock": "AAPL", "sector": "TECH", "quantity": 50, "side": "BUY" }

### 6. Add holdings directly
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/traders/T004/portfolio/holdings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "stock": "NVDA", "sector": "TECH", "quantity": 100 }

### SELL more than held -> 422 INSUFFICIENT_HOLDINGS
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "traderId": "T003", "stock": "XOM", "sector": "ENERGY", "quantity": 500, "side": "SELL" }

### Pending limit: T002 starts with 1 PENDING order; send this 3 times and the 3rd gets 422
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "traderId": "T002", "stock": "MS", "sector": "FINANCE", "quantity": 5, "side": "BUY" }
